  "evidence_limits": "1.8.1 adds a bounded experimental FC/gimbal version query on MI04, accepting only two exact DUML 00/01 frames and no retries. The uploaded Flip 1.8.0 report has eight PnP nodes and six descriptor aliases including MI04 OUT04/IN85 bulk512. The new query is bound to the selected reference ZIP by current parent product and node hashes and rechecks actual endpoints before claiming MI04. A generic DJI product string is not promoted to a marketing identity. Calibration and factory commands remain blocked; the new query has no physical Flip test yet. 1.8.0 added DJI Flip as a gimbal workshop project with firmware 01.00.1500 declared by the user, its own workspace and gimbal-scoped USB inventory. JointCoarse, LinearHall, factory and inherited operations remain blocked before any service transport because the Flip command/response and workshop-mode contract has not been validated. USB metadata is preparation only and does not implement calibration. 1.7.2 added standard descriptor inventory from the pinned libusb0 cache, bound by exact alias node to the PnP session. Enumeration may issue standard GET_DESCRIPTOR reads; no bulk transfer, interface claim, configuration write or service command is requested. Actual descriptor reading on Air 3 is not yet tested. The supplied 1.7.1 Windows report contains eight PnP nodes and product prefix e3t; this is recorded as an observation with Air 3 declared by the user, not a proven marketing alias or authenticated identity. 1.7.1 replaced the timed-out PowerShell inventory with bounded read-only CfgMgr32 calls in a supervised hidden x64 worker, preserving partial snapshots and the last native stage on timeout or cancellation. Air 3 remains a separate project target with firmware 01.00.1600 declared by the user and a Windows PnP metadata inventory. Air 3 sensor traffic and all legacy gimbal operations are blocked; no Mini 4 Pro request is reused. Firmware and reports are separated when switching models. The supplied Mini 4 Pro 1.6.0 image trial proves own x86 startup and SDK calls but contains no images: 48 wait-data timeouts over 10.209 seconds. The native timeout path was statically identified; online peers do not prove image delivery or sensor health. The Consumer initialization reference also requests a perception service start, which this receiver does not request; firmware-specific effects and complete activation contract remain unresolved. Optical calibration is not implemented for either target. Main EXE startup, UI, metadata logic, existing readers and job supervisor use synthetic or offline data under Wine; the native PnP ABI is exercised with synthetic 2-byte WCHAR fixtures in the frozen EXE. The real worker runs under Wine but its USB enumeration reports a zero-length list and is saved as an explicit error; this is not successful enumeration of a real Windows device. The user supplied a completed Windows PnP report from 1.7.1; cloud development has no physical DJI hardware and the new descriptor path is not hardware-validated. No DJI binary is redistributed or executed in cloud development."
